    "narrative": "Our lineup today is anchored by **James Wood**, who commands the highest efficiency score at 72.71. Facing a favorable matchup against Kyle Freeland, **Wood** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+14%) and the high-leverage leadoff spot, making him our primary engine for Runs and RBI. Similarly, **Brice Turang** earns a strong 67.60 rating; while his power metrics are modest, his elite ability to exploit slow pitcher deliveries\u2014bolstered by a 92% SB opportunity window\u2014makes him a critical component for our team\u2019s emphasis on stolen bases. **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Seiya Suzuki** also provide excellent stability at 66.96 and 65.63 respectively, both capitalizing on favorable park factors and high-order placements to maximize their offensive utility.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Austin Riley**. Despite a respectable 63.08 score, he narrowly missed the cut due to the superior matchup efficiency of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Isaac Paredes**, who both benefit from better-aligned platoon splits against their respective opponents. While **Riley** was on the bubble, the optimizer prioritized the high-ceiling platoon advantages presented by **Vinnie Pasquantino** and his 14% boost against right-handed pitching. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Jose Caballero**, whose low score of 41.62 puts him right at our threshold; he is strictly a volume play today, as his efficiency is heavily suppressed by an unfavorable platoon matchup and an elite opposing catcher that limits his SB upside. Ensure your lineups are finalized and monitor the wind in **McKinstry**\u2019s game, as the current forecast is the only significant atmospheric tailwind currently boosting our overall production.",
